  <section id="faq" class="section-bigger py-5 ">
    <div class="container" style="max-width: 800px;">
      <div class="text-center mb-5">
        <small class="text-uppercase text-primary d-inline-block">FAQ</small>
        <h2 class="h2 mb-2">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="faq" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/FAQPage">
                  <details class="faq"
                   itemscope
                   itemprop="mainEntity"
                   itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"
                   open>
            <summary>
              <h3 itemprop="name">What is an API credit?</h3>
            </summary>
            <div class="mt-3"
                 itemscope
                 itemprop="acceptedAnswer"
                 itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
                            <p class="lead w-text" itemprop="text">One scrape costs a variable number of credits depending on the configuration. HTTP scrape on a datacenter IP is 1 credit; adding browser rendering or residential proxies increases the cost. See the credit-cost table above, or the <a href="/docs/billing">full matrix in the docs</a>.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
                  <details class="faq"
                   itemscope
                   itemprop="mainEntity"
                   itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"
                   >
            <summary>
              <h3 itemprop="name">What happens when I hit my monthly quota?</h3>
            </summary>
            <div class="mt-3"
                 itemscope
                 itemprop="acceptedAnswer"
                 itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
                            <p class="lead w-text" itemprop="text">From Pro and up, you switch to pay-as-you-go at the per-10k-credit rate on your plan, your integration never stalls. Discovery caps on quota for a predictable bill; upgrade to Pro from the dashboard if you need overflow. If pay-as-you-go consistently makes the next plan up cheaper, upgrade in one click.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
                  <details class="faq"
                   itemscope
                   itemprop="mainEntity"
                   itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"
                   >
            <summary>
              <h3 itemprop="name">Can I change or cancel my subscription?</h3>
            </summary>
            <div class="mt-3"
                 itemscope
                 itemprop="acceptedAnswer"
                 itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
                            <p class="lead w-text" itemprop="text">Yes. Upgrade, downgrade, or cancel any time from the dashboard. Downgrade and cancel take effect at the end of the current billing period, so you get every credit you paid for.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
                  <details class="faq"
                   itemscope
                   itemprop="mainEntity"
                   itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"
                   >
            <summary>
              <h3 itemprop="name">Do unused credits roll over?</h3>
            </summary>
            <div class="mt-3"
                 itemscope
                 itemprop="acceptedAnswer"
                 itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
                            <p class="lead w-text" itemprop="text">No. Quotas reset at renewal. If you consistently end the month with leftovers, downgrade to a smaller plan and use pay-as-you-go for the occasional overflow. You end up paying less.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
                  <details class="faq"
                   itemscope
                   itemprop="mainEntity"
                   itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"
                   >
            <summary>
              <h3 itemprop="name">Is the free tier time-limited?</h3>
            </summary>
            <div class="mt-3"
                 itemscope
                 itemprop="acceptedAnswer"
                 itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
                            <p class="lead w-text" itemprop="text">No. 1,000 credits on signup, no card required, every product usable. Keep the free key forever for smoke tests and prototypes.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
                  <details class="faq"
                   itemscope
                   itemprop="mainEntity"
                   itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"
                   >
            <summary>
              <h3 itemprop="name">Do you offer custom or enterprise plans?</h3>
            </summary>
            <div class="mt-3"
                 itemscope
                 itemprop="acceptedAnswer"
                 itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
                            <p class="lead w-text" itemprop="text">Yes, above 5.5M credits per month. Custom plans include volume discounts, dedicated proxy pools, committed concurrency, premium support, and a signed DPA. <a href="mailto:sales@scrapfly.io?subject=Custom%20Plan%20Request">Contact sales</a>.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
              </div>
    </div>
  </section>

